.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-payments-transactions - List on-chain transactions for a payment


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 payments transactions  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List the on-chain transactions a payment has produced, one row per attempt,
newest first by default.

.PP
This is the view -w/--wait watches: it polls THIS table for the attempt it
created and returns when that row reads confirmed or failed. So it is also
where to look when a --wait timed out, or when an operation was submitted
without one — the row's status says whether the chain has spoken yet, and a
failed row carries the decoded revert reason.

.PP
A payment can hold several rows for the same operation (a retried broadcast, or
successive partial captures), which is why the balances a payment reports are
the last CONFIRMED ones and not the last submitted.

.PP
--status takes several values, repeated or comma-separated, and matches ANY of
them: '--status submitting,submitted' is what is on its way to the chain.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for transactions

.PP
\fB--operation\fP=""
	Filter by operation (authorize, charge, capture, void, release, refund, dispute, close_dispute)

.PP
\fB--page\fP=0
	Page number (1-based)

.PP
\fB--per-page\fP=0
	Results per page

.PP
\fB--sort\fP=""
	Sort fields: created_at, updated_at, block_number, confirmed_at (prefix - for descending, comma-separated)

.PP
\fB--status\fP=[]
	Filter by transaction status (pending, submitting, submitted, confirmed, failed); repeat or comma-separate for any of several


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--agent\fP[=false]
	Agent mode: one JSON envelope on stdout, JSON events on stderr, no prompts (env: RAIL0_AGENT=1)

.PP
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 payments transactions 0xabc123…
  rail0 payments transactions 0xabc123… --sort -confirmed_at
  rail0 payments transactions 0xabc123… --operation capture --status failed
  rail0 payments transactions 0xabc123… --status submitting,submitted
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-payments(1)\fP
